{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>But if a creation, etc.</b> He doubled the expression, saying <b>a creation that HaShem will create</b>. This may be explained according to the way our Sages of blessed memory expounded it (Sanhedrin 37b) regarding the verse ״cursed... is the ground which opened its mouth״ — that from that day on the mouth of the earth was sealed and closed, and when it wishes to sing song before HaShem in the manner of all created beings that sing song before the Creator, it says so with its wing, as it is written (Isaiah 24:16) ״from the wing of the earth we heard songs.״ And here, when Moses wished to punish those wicked men, he said <b>but if a creation</b> — meaning, that creation that HaShem had already made, namely the mouth of the earth, which through the act [of the flood] was sealed and became as though it had never been — now HaShem will return to create that creation, so that it will have a mouth, and the earth will open its mouth that it formerly had, and swallow them. And perhaps, for this will be its rectification for having opened [its mouth] to swallow a righteous man — now it will open its mouth to swallow the enemies of HaShem."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase מַעֲשֶׂה נִסְתַּם (\"through the act it was sealed\") likely alludes to the earth's mouth being sealed since the generation of the flood, per the Sanhedrin passage just cited; rendered hyper-literally as the syntax is slightly compressed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:30.691252433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}